<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian July export prices fell 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian July export prices fell 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian export prices fell 0.1 percent in July from the previous month and were 7.6 percent lower than July 1995, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Lower world market prices led to decreases in the price of aluminium and aluminium goods. Prices of mineral fuels and oils fell during the month,&quot; the bureau said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Partially offsetting these decreases was an increase in the price of wool.&quot;</p>
<p>The export price index has been in steady monthly decline since a 0.7 percent increase in January, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Canberra bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
